  {
   "id": "ja3-6",
   "title": "The て-form",
   "unit": "Unit 2 · The て-form",
   "learn": [
    {
     "h": "The most useful verb form",
     "p": "The <b>て-form</b> links actions and makes requests. る-verbs just swap る for て (たべる → たべて). Others change sound: のむ → のんで, いく → いって, する → して. Add <b>ください</b> and it becomes a polite request: たべて ください = please eat.",
     "ex": [
      "ja-たべて",
      "ja-のんで",
      "ja-たべて ください。"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "ja-たべて",
     "w": "たべて",
     "r": "tabete",
     "m": "eat (て-form)",
     "kind": "word"
    },
    {
     "id": "ja-みて",
     "w": "みて",
     "r": "mite",
     "m": "look (て-form)",
     "kind": "word"
    },
    {
     "id": "ja-きいて",
     "w": "きいて",
     "r": "kiite",
     "m": "listen (て-form)",
     "kind": "word"
    },
